1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,860
Welcome back to Level Six!

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:08,620
Last time we walked down Word Family Lane, and you read eighty-one words.

3
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:10,460
Do you remember

4
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,000
the trick?

5
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:16,880
If you can read the ending, you only need to find the letter at the front.

6
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:23,580
Today we are going to practise, and this is exactly the game the app plays with you.

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:24,840
It is

8
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,280
called Find the First Letter.

9
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:29,560
Here is how it works.

10
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:34,810
I will show you a picture, and a word with its first letter missing.

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,830
You will see three letters.

12
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,120
Only one of them is right.

13
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,520
Say your answer out loud.

14
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:45,420
Ready?

15
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:47,080
Let's warm up.

16
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,560
We will start at the house you know best.

17
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,580
The ‑at family.

18
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:54,930
Here is the picture.

19
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:57,300
A cat.

20
00:00:58,900 --> 00:00:59,960
And here is the word.

21
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:02,440
Something…

22
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:03,260
at.

23
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,340
Which letter starts this word?

24
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:12,260
Is it b, c, or h?

25
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:15,700
C!

26
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:17,140
C…

27
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:17,840
at.

28
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:19,500
Cat.

29
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:21,420
Well done!

30
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:23,980
Next picture.

31
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,320
A bat.

32
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:28,120
Something…

33
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:28,700
at again.

34
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:32,780
Which letter starts it?

35
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,760
B, c, or r?

36
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:38,680
B!

37
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,440
B…

38
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,060
at.

39
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:42,800
Bat.

40
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:44,700
That was quick!

41
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:47,140
Here is a hat.

42
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:52,760
Which letter — c, m, or h?

43
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:55,540
H!

44
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:56,580
Hat.

45
00:01:57,620 --> 00:01:58,320
You are on fire.

46
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:01,620
One more from this family.

47
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:03,440
A rat!

48
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:09,720
Which letter — c, r, or f?

49
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:12,660
R!

50
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:13,820
Rat.

51
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,180
Four out of four.

52
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:19,400
The ‑at family is easy for you now.

53
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:25,120
If you are enjoying this, please tap like and subscribe — it really helps us.

54
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,200
Now, let's keep going!

55
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:31,600
Let's visit two more houses.

56
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:33,240
Same game.

57
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:35,610
Here is a fan.

58
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,140
Something…

59
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,140
an.

60
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:45,220
Which letter — m, v, or f?

61
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,100
F!

62
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:49,720
Fan.

63
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:51,060
Lovely.

64
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,940
And here is a van.

65
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:59,420
Which letter — v, f, or m?

66
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:02,500
V!

67
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:03,960
Van.

68
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:08,200
Fan and van — only the front changed.

69
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:09,900
You spotted it.

70
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:12,680
Now the ‑en house.

71
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:14,920
Here is a hen.

72
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:20,200
Which letter — p, h, or t?

73
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,080
H!

74
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:24,380
Hen.

75
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:26,460
And here is a pen.

76
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:32,420
Which letter — d, p, or h?

77
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:34,720
Hmm.

78
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:36,100
Is it d?

79
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:37,880
D…

80
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,240
en.

81
00:03:40,410 --> 00:03:40,960
Den.

82
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,030
But look at the picture.

83
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:46,550
That is not a den, that is a pen!

84
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,800
So it is p.

85
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:50,640
P…

86
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,720
en.

87
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,120
Pen.

88
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:57,600
Good try — and that is exactly what to do.

89
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,380
If the word you build

90
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:02,680
does not match the picture, try another letter.

91
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:04,740
That is not a mistake.

92
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,480
That is checking.

93
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:09,670
You are ready for the quick round.

94
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:13,020
Six pictures, six different families.

95
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,360
Say the letter as

96
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:16,760
fast as you can.

97
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:18,520
A dog!

98
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:22,260
L, f, or d?

99
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:24,400
D!

100
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:25,560
Dog.

101
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,100
A pig!

102
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:31,060
P, b, or d?

103
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,460
P!

104
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:34,380
Pig.

105
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:36,100
A pot!

106
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:40,060
H, p, or d?

107
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:42,220
P!

108
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:43,040
Pot.

109
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,230
The sun!

110
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:48,900
R, f, or s?

111
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:51,340
S!

112
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:53,040
Sun.

113
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:54,740
A map!

114
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:58,760
M, c, or n?

115
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:00,600
M!

116
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:01,640
Map.

117
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:04,040
Last one.

118
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,380
A jug!

119
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,220
B, j, or r?

120
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:11,520
J!

121
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:12,620
Jug.

122
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:15,340
You finished the quick round!

123
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:16,970
Look at your score.

124
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:21,460
Fourteen questions, and you answered every single one.

125
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,530
Do you see what happened?

126
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,860
You did not sound out fourteen whole words.

127
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,590
You read the ending,

128
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:32,200
found the front, and the word was just…

129
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:32,760
there.

130
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:35,170
That is what practice does.

131
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:37,600
I am so proud of you.

132
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:40,220
Level Six is yours now.

133
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:46,460
Play Find the First Letter in the English Learning app — it mixes the questions up every

134
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:49,540
time, so it is never the same game twice.

135
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:55,020
The English Learning app is free on the Apple App Store and Google Play.

136
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:58,460
Next time, a brand new adventure.

137
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,640
Don't miss it!

138
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,800
See you next time!
